# Region_Connections.mmd

## Purpose
A graph of the connections between the locations within a single region, and any locations in neighboring regions they physically connect to.

## Context
Consult when drafting:
- `GENRE.md` - mythic underworld means layout should read as decayed and found, not architected as a puzzle box aimed at the party.
- this region's `Locations.md` - the locations being connected.

## Instructions
Unlike `setting/Connections.mmd` (region-level, existence only), this diagram may be directional and should indicate different connection types where they matter to how a party moves through the region.

Connection type reference:
- `A --- B` normal - an open, two-way passage or path
- `A -.- B` hidden - a concealed, sealed, or secret connection
- `A --> B` one-way - only traversable in the direction shown

## Template
```mermaid
graph LR
    A1["[Code] [Location Name]"] --- A2["[Code] [Location Name]"]
    A2 -.- A3["[Code] [Location Name]"]
    A3 --> A4["[Code] [Location Name]"]
```
